From: Alex Ayars <aayars@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 23:34:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 06/29] export kit: claim only effects the parity sweep
 verified; retry load-induced timeouts alone

Backend admission says a kernel exists for every pass, not that the effect
renders exactly across its parameter domain: the kit listed effects that
refuse every non-default define value. export-kit/verified-effects.json is
derived by tools/parity/verified_effects.py from sweep results (every
single-effect case byte-exact on RGBA8 and float32, or refused by both
sides), and generate-compat.mjs lists only those effects. From the 20-variant
and define-enumeration sweeps of this tree: 137 verified effects (the
admission-only list claimed 167).

sweep.py now reruns a timed-out case alone with 4x the budget before
reporting it, so a loaded machine cannot turn a slow case into a failure
while a real hang still fails the gate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
